  },
  {
    q: 'Am I in the homeowners association?',
    a: 'Check your deed, because in a neighbourhood built across four decades the answer genuinely varies. The association\'s recorded documents include restrictions and covenants from 1988, restated covenants the same year, an assessment notice from 1993, and — the interesting one — an election extending annexation rights recorded in 1998. That last instrument is the mechanism by which later sections were brought into the same association. Its existence tells you that coverage was extended deliberately over time rather than applying automatically to everything named Grassland Estates, which is exactly why it is worth confirming rather than assuming.',
  },
  {
    q: 'There is a park in the middle of the neighbourhood. Does that change anything?',
    a: 'A little, and it is worth knowing which direction pressure comes from. Grasslands Park on Crowley Boulevard is five acres with a pavilion, benches, picnic tables and bins, sitting inside the platted area. Five acres of maintained, watered turf in a region averaging around fourteen inches of rain a year is a concentrator: it suits imported fire ants, it supports a much larger population of crickets and other prey insects than the ground around it, and that prey base draws scorpions and spiders toward whatever boundary the park shares. The bins add a small, steady refuse point that interests rodents. If your lot backs onto it, that is your active boundary and perimeter work there is worth more than the same effort spread evenly.',
  },
  {
